{number: 69}
{title: ‘Tis So Sweet to Trust in Jesus}
{key: Ab}

{start_of_verse: 1}
[Ab] 'Tis so sweet to trust in Jesus,
Just to take Him at His [Eb7] word;
[Ab] Just to rest upon His promise,
Just to [Eb7] know, "Thus saith the [Ab] Lord."
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_chorus}
[Ab] Jesus, Jesus, how I trust Him!
How I've proved Him o'er and [Eb7] o'er!
[Ab] Jesus, Jesus, precious Jesus!
O for [Eb7] grace to trust Him [Ab] more!
{end_of_chorus}

{start_of_verse: 2}
O how [Ab] sweet to trust in Jesus,
Just to trust His cleansing [Eb7] blood;
[Ab] Just in simple faith to plunge me
'Neath the [Eb7] healing, cleansing [Ab] flood!
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 3}
Yes, 'tis [Ab] sweet to trust in Jesus,
Just from sin and self to [Eb7] cease;
[Ab] Just from Jesus simply taking
Life and [Eb7] rest, and joy and [Ab] peace.
{end_of_verse}

{start_of_verse: 4}
I'm so [Ab] glad I learned to trust Thee,
Precious Jesus, Savior, [Eb7] Friend;
And I [Ab] know that Thou art with me,
Wilt be [Eb7] with me to the [Ab] end.
{end_of_verse}
